No maintainer secret key was available to export in this checkout.

Before the first protected release, export the armored public key:

```sh
gpg --armor --export <maintainer-release-key-fingerprint> \
  > docs/release-signing.asc
gpg --show-keys --with-fingerprint docs/release-signing.asc
```

Commit `docs/release-signing.asc`. Never commit the private key. The release
workflow deliberately fails closed while that required public-key file is
absent, empty, invalid, or cannot populate the job's GPG keyring.
